[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171898 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/id #uuid "91f986c6-c305-50eb-a5b7-36043279d128" :question/math-academy-id "e-9505" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle \\mathbf{T}_1 : {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ v\\end{array} \\right]} \\longrightarrow {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u + v \\\\ v - 2 u + 1\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle \\mathbf{T}_2 : {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ v\\end{array} \\right]} \\longrightarrow {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u - v \\\\ v - u\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle \\mathbf{T}_3 : {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ v\\end{array} \\right]} \\longrightarrow {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ u - {v}^{2}\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_1$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_1$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ v-2u+1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ -2u+v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_2$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}u-v \\\\ v-u\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u-v \\\\ -u+v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_3$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic term $v^2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$\\mathbf{T}_1$ and $\\mathbf{T}_2$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171899 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172093 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/id #uuid "9779a982-2048-58e2-8a90-df2bcb366d96" :question/math-academy-id "e-9506" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 5u + v - 6, \\qquad y = 2u + 4v\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]} = \n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}5 & \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{a} \\\\ \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{b} & 4\\end{array} \\right]} \\cdot {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ v\\end{array} \\right]}+\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 6 \\\\ \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{c}\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]} \n= {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}5 u + v - 6 \\\\ 2 u + 4 v\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5u+v-6 \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5u+v \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+2+0 = 3.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171900 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172094 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/id #uuid "2ddc4e15-3729-5425-953c-1cb95edc201b" :question/math-academy-id "e-9508" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 3u-v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{a}, \\qquad y = u + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{b}v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{c}\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]} = \n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}3 & - 1 \\\\ 1 & - 5\\end{array} \\right]} \\cdot {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ v\\end{array} \\right]}+\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ 0\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}}^{A}\\cdot \\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}^{u}+\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{b} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3u-v \\\\ u-5v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3u-v+1 \\\\ u-5v\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx = 3u - v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{1}, \\qquad y = u + (\\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{-5})v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{0} \\, .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+(-5)+0 = -4.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25af0a87-182e-5990-bff6-4172cecd65e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257101} {:answer/id #uuid "7263de35-2e64-59d5-bed2-c6826d238737" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257786} {:answer/id #uuid "a965f12a-4008-5c40-a980-4436e558b445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258260} {:answer/id #uuid "eecbdb0e-1aed-51b7-9d8e-33c52edd3e69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258852} {:answer/id #uuid "f174307d-f40b-5af3-89dc-5531ccdb867d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a965f12a-4008-5c40-a980-4436e558b445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258260} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfbec513-c207-593e-beb2-a6680e010d0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4d581310-6942-54b8-b545-b203d0da1352" :question/math-academy-id "q-124007" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ v-u\\end{bmatrix}$\n- ${T}_{2}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{2} \\\\ -v\\end{bmatrix}$\n- ${T}_{3}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+2 \\\\ u-v+1\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ v-u\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ -u+v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{1}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic term ${u}^{2}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+2 \\\\ u-v+1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ u-v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172294 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172093 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6609faf5-218c-5c18-93e2-43f7844cd543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257682} {:answer/id #uuid "7bb52f73-b59b-5559-a1a9-0a3e40afda0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257877} {:answer/id #uuid "b7bcc0cb-9c0c-5351-b203-fb02bf523336" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258387} {:answer/id #uuid "d1f6db9c-5b9d-5bd9-a019-2b86dc159910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258611} {:answer/id #uuid "d6ab26a8-fcba-5abc-9df8-f8a6a45e0da4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6609faf5-218c-5c18-93e2-43f7844cd543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257682} :answer-field/id #uuid "471f200c-b9c9-5e1b-b46b-262099bea64a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b49d315-187b-5a70-8690-97b6311cd839" :question/math-academy-id "q-124088" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=u-2v+1,\\,y=u+v-2\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}u-2v+1 \\\\ u+v-2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}u-2v+1 \\\\ u+v-2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u-2v \\\\ u+v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+(-2)+(-2)=-3.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172094 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "003c72ab-a274-52ab-aa2c-2593da45d334" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256784} {:answer/id #uuid "7e750f7c-8312-5236-a7f3-e877f7f70512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257905} {:answer/id #uuid "a6ab775c-a099-5165-bdb5-243b28bd32ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258236} {:answer/id #uuid "dee951d0-1321-54ed-8801-95e0057779e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258724} {:answer/id #uuid "eb76beb7-5c43-55e3-8818-e328ff068342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258822}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e750f7c-8312-5236-a7f3-e877f7f70512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257905} :answer-field/id #uuid "62c09496-ed8d-5b09-8ce6-b28b1163e1a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "01d5649d-0bb8-52a3-be74-234b60c39fb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-124091" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=-u+av+b,\\,y=2u-5v+c\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}}^{A}\\cdot \\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}^{u}+\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{b} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-u+4v \\\\ 2u-5v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-u+4v+2 \\\\ 2u-5v+1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=-u+4v+2,\\,y=2u-5v+1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=4+2+1=7.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172296 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "255ddd21-b1c5-5d8e-b4ad-aac9373b3095" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257098} {:answer/id #uuid "4a828879-d0fe-5d7a-8b54-7fab93033af5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257432} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd652bd-48bd-5bb8-8102-3594c7c7c1b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257748} {:answer/id #uuid "b6f28373-fae0-549e-9a0b-3785d4466329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258377} {:answer/id #uuid "be256b1b-d3ab-5059-b1c7-8f3112a90e36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a828879-d0fe-5d7a-8b54-7fab93033af5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257432} :answer-field/id #uuid "d67d9325-f611-53e9-98be-67d533821ecc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c5cb4053-f0cc-5e78-b06a-329e6bd661d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-124255" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}v-7u+3 \\\\ 3v-u+1\\end{bmatrix}$\n- ${T}_{2}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}uv+1 \\\\ u-2v\\end{bmatrix}$\n- ${T}_{3}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}9u \\\\ u-v\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}v-7u+3 \\\\ 3v-u+1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7u+v \\\\ -u+3v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}9u \\\\ u-v\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9u \\\\ u-v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{3}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172297 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172094 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "051434b8-c984-5c6a-8955-1f0b60930d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256829} {:answer/id #uuid "2752c7eb-4676-56ab-b0cd-1bf9a38e162f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257126} {:answer/id #uuid "59eb0a37-274e-5830-8b80-ff23964f5119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257562} {:answer/id #uuid "81280065-bedd-5f73-8e81-255309fdda87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257929} {:answer/id #uuid "e993acbd-20a6-5dc9-8643-05cf5a9fa4b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e993acbd-20a6-5dc9-8643-05cf5a9fa4b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258811} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0be749e-1222-5271-990b-b7537ef677e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9882bc48-ffe2-5a96-827b-d1eb44c92577" :question/math-academy-id "q-124271" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+4v,\\,y=-5u+bv+c\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{A}\\cdot \\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}^{u}+\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{b} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3u+4v \\\\ -5u+3v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3u+4v \\\\ -5u+3v\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=-3u+4v,\\,y=-5u+3v+0\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-3+3+0=0.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172298 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172093 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2565bba5-5eac-5cdf-86de-6ce6f7d0d3b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257099} {:answer/id #uuid "3ba6f2e5-650b-5a1e-987d-fbf362041044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257314} {:answer/id #uuid "6ccad9ff-665f-52f7-90d6-bb242d608429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257741} {:answer/id #uuid "6ebaf9c7-1edf-584c-8b9b-b5af17d2eab7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257758} {:answer/id #uuid "bd4687f8-a5a9-54bc-b0a0-64f52c2b2036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ba6f2e5-650b-5a1e-987d-fbf362041044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257314} :answer-field/id #uuid "498afc40-c208-5e2f-a071-6c4f2ca45dea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c8d697d1-ccf8-518a-9776-12fda551dcda" :question/math-academy-id "q-124291" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=5u+3,\\,y=7v-u\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ b & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5u+3 \\\\ 7v-u\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5u+3 \\\\ 7v-u\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5u \\\\ -u+7v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=5+(-1)+3=7.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259630 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f3b4ff8-e9b0-521b-a9c7-8ce613488d5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257459} {:answer/id #uuid "81a82df1-73ea-5ee2-b9f4-cd8efef245d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257935} {:answer/id #uuid "971b265b-627d-584c-8bd5-b975e9552229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258115} {:answer/id #uuid "a4ffc45a-0a6d-5af5-aff4-9edb51326307" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258220} {:answer/id #uuid "b7fd1e66-1022-5d36-99e4-76b9bc2be555" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "971b265b-627d-584c-8bd5-b975e9552229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258115} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fd515da-2bfd-5ed1-b4e6-947a8a071af9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259147}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd962593-19ff-5124-a324-851d683c9d53" :question/math-academy-id "q-124236" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ \\sqrt{v}\\end{bmatrix}$\n- ${T}_{2}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+1 \\\\ {v}^{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\n- ${T}_{3}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}3u-2 \\\\ 8-v\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not affine since it contains the term $\\sqrt{v}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the cubic term ${v}^{3}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3u-2 \\\\ 8-v\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3u \\\\ -v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{3}$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259631 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3af05d3e-30eb-5918-91db-aa8c3a197237" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257304} {:answer/id #uuid "3e616a32-d29b-5f08-93ed-071ac16b3da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257342} {:answer/id #uuid "7dce96d6-a180-5c14-a0e1-d3830ccaa2d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257895} {:answer/id #uuid "c144722c-9c7d-5454-80ab-16bbb5e3cf27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258472} {:answer/id #uuid "f753729a-b8ab-5b2d-bbfc-716c8a2bfb27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e616a32-d29b-5f08-93ed-071ac16b3da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257342} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5d330ca-85d9-55ae-bc23-193deb6c6d8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "61d7ee8c-7043-59bf-884d-8cfd140d0d17" :question/math-academy-id "q-124237" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}v-6u+7 \\\\ 4u+3v-5\\end{bmatrix}$\n- ${T}_{2}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{bmatrix}$\n- ${T}_{3}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2u+v \\\\ uv+1\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}v-6u+7 \\\\ 4u+3v-5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6u+v \\\\ 4u+3v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{2}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4de0082d-50c4-5d80-b063-91bd017a1545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257451} {:answer/id #uuid "5d087fdf-6d61-58c5-b78e-6d419b6ee799" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257591} {:answer/id #uuid "739355b8-4721-5999-8150-50c1a6ed20d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257795} {:answer/id #uuid "bdbd9f1e-6203-5220-b685-f660d3c02c7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258436} {:answer/id #uuid "f2e1ae10-e87c-57e1-a5df-1f35cce54260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d087fdf-6d61-58c5-b78e-6d419b6ee799" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257591} :answer-field/id #uuid "513f8367-607c-5e96-9439-18e4d01f3c9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a803158d-6736-5561-9888-f16b39fbcde9" :question/math-academy-id "q-124245" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}7u-v+6 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}$\n- ${T}_{2}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}8v-9u \\\\ 4u-v\\end{bmatrix}$\n- ${T}_{3}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u-5 \\\\ 8u\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}7u-v+6 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7u-v \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8v-9u \\\\ 4u-v\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9u+8v \\\\ 4u-v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{2}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}u-5 \\\\ 8u\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ 8u\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}.$\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b2cf13d-a183-5e14-a4b5-462bfd278b09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257166} {:answer/id #uuid "4f6a73e3-8d6c-5cde-8f8b-f62b5997fb77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257463} {:answer/id #uuid "a8cfc09f-e2ab-5d00-aa5b-f5e739273487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258254} {:answer/id #uuid "cb15038f-1ec4-5f28-aec7-ea630c2ddb0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258545} {:answer/id #uuid "f0be6935-9d30-5bdd-83ef-ea913d0881f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8cfc09f-e2ab-5d00-aa5b-f5e739273487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258254} :answer-field/id #uuid "604b8e22-70c6-57af-b395-f873faa084c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f56913d5-4faa-5365-a00a-436d31c63ba7" :question/math-academy-id "q-124247" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{bmatrix}$\n- ${T}_{2}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ 1-{v}^{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\n- ${T}_{3}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u(v-1) \\\\ u-1\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{1}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the cubic term ${v}^{3}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259637 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b02e3f-baf3-57d3-a076-ab452fdeef0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256799} {:answer/id #uuid "22814352-2c48-5958-9dee-a9a29d563b86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257066} {:answer/id #uuid "27a5552d-e286-524b-8546-cef93fa80826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257133} {:answer/id #uuid "2f4661b6-b14e-5456-9974-00d318903de3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257199} {:answer/id #uuid "f916b4e3-4292-594a-9059-6b10083c974a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22814352-2c48-5958-9dee-a9a29d563b86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257066} :answer-field/id #uuid "206fb4ee-adb0-528a-87ee-8ada6b197a84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "13d7af34-5a26-56da-8335-dcbefb3a99a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-124251" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{2}-{v}^{2} \\\\ v-u\\end{bmatrix}$\n- ${T}_{2}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}6v-4u \\\\ 3u+3v\\end{bmatrix}$\n- ${T}_{3}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+v+9 \\\\ v-9\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic terms ${u}^{2}$ and ${v}^{2}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6v-4u \\\\ 3u+3v\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4u+6v \\\\ 3u+3v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{2}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+v+9 \\\\ v-9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172092 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "256fbf73-68d8-56cd-99d4-6ab220700234" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257100} {:answer/id #uuid "3df03890-7218-544f-a1c1-3ad95cf59941" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257334} {:answer/id #uuid "5e8dddff-e30a-5e35-99d4-ea31f8bef8de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257613} {:answer/id #uuid "ad08e75f-d6b2-5f74-b630-c7824215bf61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258294} {:answer/id #uuid "fce36429-baf1-517b-9f7f-64595779152d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "256fbf73-68d8-56cd-99d4-6ab220700234" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257100} :answer-field/id #uuid "63e916b1-34bb-5434-90d1-69e05a02c05b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d494b59f-56bb-56d7-a682-8c7f88848b2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-124253" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u-1 \\\\ {e}^{v}\\end{bmatrix}$\n- ${T}_{2}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}8u+2v+2 \\\\ u-2v+4\\end{bmatrix}$\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {T}_{3}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not affine since it contains the exponential term ${e}^{v}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8u+2v+2 \\\\ u-2v+4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8u+2v \\\\ u-2v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the term $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{2}$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259639 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172094 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "227340af-71d1-5d08-ace5-1c9258c8fcf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257065} {:answer/id #uuid "30bb3807-55a5-5cda-b326-fdec9c047352" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257211} {:answer/id #uuid "41438c81-cf63-57d7-afc0-35b56a8a92f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257363} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb37718-f272-5547-a58a-87b172f20251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258850} {:answer/id #uuid "ffd38fa9-a703-5a9b-9e62-e43d804d84e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eeb37718-f272-5547-a58a-87b172f20251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258850} :answer-field/id #uuid "e68f436c-5c06-5c77-ab1f-cbf71cb2e171" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "248bc276-68c1-5b41-9594-c7af8b2e1b35" :question/math-academy-id "q-124259" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+bv+3,\\,y=-9u+cv+4\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}^{A}\\cdot \\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}^{u}+\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}^{b} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ -9u+4v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u+3 \\\\ -9u+4v+4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=1u+0v+3,\\,y=-9u+4v+4\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+0+4=5.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259640 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172094 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e740d3a-5c03-5dd2-816a-487643106091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257194} {:answer/id #uuid "33a79aaa-17fe-5ec0-9815-f48d8949b65f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257239} {:answer/id #uuid "73970941-5456-5fe8-906f-5e233465ae16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257796} {:answer/id #uuid "9158f20d-6a83-542a-9c54-77af73ba69ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258067} {:answer/id #uuid "ce7c1236-c621-5444-b1e2-cd41e1db1cdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce7c1236-c621-5444-b1e2-cd41e1db1cdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258575} :answer-field/id #uuid "671307a9-23d3-54b5-988a-ecf7a2f8a2ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259210}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ded880b4-9f04-5275-85c1-4486642a0a7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-124261" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+bv-2,\\,y=u+c\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{A}\\cdot \\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}^{u}+\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}^{b} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6u+8v \\\\ u\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6u+8v-2 \\\\ u+5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=6u+8v-2,\\,y=u+5\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=6+8+5=19.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172094 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fe1c6ee-1822-5943-a4ab-95e2e8729c1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257204} {:answer/id #uuid "42afdead-f7ba-55b9-837b-58a7ebcab735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257371} {:answer/id #uuid "5b54affb-22be-504f-9fc3-75ecc52418c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257578} {:answer/id #uuid "d4002265-2697-5e13-a97a-e4de62345ee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258638} {:answer/id #uuid "f3d00b3d-b50a-5be5-8ad2-4acce9512f8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 175921862589